<title>AUSTRALIA: NSW deputy premier to oppose electricity selloff.</title>
<headline>NSW deputy premier to oppose electricity selloff.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-05-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>New South Wales deputy premier Andrew Refshauge said on Friday he was opposed to Treasurer Michael Egan's proposed privatisation of the electricity system.</p>
<p>When asked on Australian Broadcasting Corp radio whether he would support the selloff, Refshauge, a leading light of the left faction in the Labor party, said he would argue against it.</p>
<p>Egan circulated a state Treasury discussion paper on Thursday that outlined plans to raise up to A$22 billion through the sale of power stations, distributors, transmission lines and a stake in the Snowy Mountains Hydroelectric Authority.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
